    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## clarvia.jobs.dispatch.v1\n\n**Purpose:** Lease pending automation jobs from `clarvia.automation_jobs` and dispatch each to the appropriate internal Next.js endpoint by topic. Triggered by an internal webhook kick (from webhook ingress `after()`) and a 1-minute schedule fallback.\n\n**Input contract:**\n- Webhook kick: POST to `/dispatch-kick` (empty body, used as wake-up signal)\n- Schedule: every 1 minute\n\n**Output contract:** None. Each job is completed or failed via the internal jobs API. PostgreSQL manages durable retry scheduling.\n\n**Topic routing:**\n- `stripe.event.process` → `/api/internal/automation/stripe/process`\n- `nurture.enrol` → `/api/internal/automation/nurture/enrol`\n- `email.send` → `/api/internal/automation/email/send`\n- `reconciliation.run` → `/api/internal/automation/reconciliation/run`\n- Unknown → dead-letter with `UNKNOWN_TOPIC`\n\n**Owner:** Clarvia automation team.\n\n**Credentials:**\n- `clarvia-internal-api` — HMAC auth for all internal API calls (§5.3)\n- `clarvia-sentry-webhook` — Sentry webhook for dead-letter alerts\n\n**Env vars:**\n- `CLARVIA_INTERNAL_URL` — base URL for internal API\n- `CLARVIA_INTERNAL_HMAC_SECRET` — HMAC signing secret\n- `CLARVIA_SENTRY_WEBHOOK_URL` — Sentry ingest endpoint",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 560
      },
      "id": "d1e2f3a4-0002-4a00-8000-000000000018",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [100, 20]
    }
  ],
